[{:db/id "q-10074/selection/4a78c79ebc3ccf6677ffb2b4326e9bc0e0a08c6580fdd5acf8b2d0ceff7d5db9" :answer/id #uuid "7f7fbde2-1a21-5fb1-8d83-65e0637b0829" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-15,y=-10,z=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074/selection/69287ec85e1a864180896cf86165ddef5b29a5edfdd76b2900412b34794f4165" :answer/id #uuid "42da5cbf-1dcc-5f8e-aff0-1ee1c79574da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-30,y=-20,z=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074/selection/677dea8567434c1de5af23e65bd5c7337dde04fbca7d2b417ddd345fcadd7bc4" :answer/id #uuid "d49ea752-b50e-5647-ba94-f4bf5951285c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074/selection/3bdf864cb71d919e94f73a7538f31d832de1152326827617edb7c2ed150610dd" :answer/id #uuid "3913b813-19e1-5838-a7ce-25c5f75b98b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{15}{11},y=\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074/selection/fe208a1de33727750b42d5767ea06a0c736d95e10c0a41aca9da10f2aa2235cd" :answer/id #uuid "5fdb890a-69a1-5c8a-b553-5afded12115b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=15,y=10,z=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed131fa2-13cf-592a-be0c-f93fee5f0963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10074/selection/677dea8567434c1de5af23e65bd5c7337dde04fbca7d2b417ddd345fcadd7bc4" :answer-field/choices ["q-10074/selection/4a78c79ebc3ccf6677ffb2b4326e9bc0e0a08c6580fdd5acf8b2d0ceff7d5db9" "q-10074/selection/69287ec85e1a864180896cf86165ddef5b29a5edfdd76b2900412b34794f4165" "q-10074/selection/677dea8567434c1de5af23e65bd5c7337dde04fbca7d2b417ddd345fcadd7bc4" "q-10074/selection/3bdf864cb71d919e94f73a7538f31d832de1152326827617edb7c2ed150610dd" "q-10074/selection/fe208a1de33727750b42d5767ea06a0c736d95e10c0a41aca9da10f2aa2235cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10074" :question/id #uuid "e436b484-45cd-5959-9069-2880512ec233" :question/math-academy-id "q-10074" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z=-1-x \\\\ 4y=-5z \\\\ x+6z-3=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=-1 \\\\ 4y+5z=0 \\\\ x+6z=3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(24)-2(-5)+3(0-4) \\\\  & =24+10-12 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}24 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 12 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}24 & 5 & -4 \\\\ -12 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}24 & -12 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{15}{11} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{11} \\\\ \\frac{8}{11}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{15}{11},y=-\\frac{10}{11},z=\\frac{8}{11}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10074/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10074"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" :answer/id #uuid "145a2179-7b72-57df-bff7-80d3502f28f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={B}^{-1}{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" :answer/id #uuid "0d158e3a-4d89-5a89-9079-ebfc9750e6bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=BA\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection/710362311ddc3bc52513e1e2ddc794521971553b13e2205991db2c922f009345" :answer/id #uuid "23189103-9802-5ea2-97a6-08d94623c558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B\\,d\\,A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection/e472aecf20d2cd5f0e251ef5d584b24ad0b47241a56a31d04ed07656c00b18c1" :answer/id #uuid "a03d7fc3-1cb8-5c99-ae8d-a93c40d4daad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=B{A}^{-1}\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0" :answer/id #uuid "75cd0fcc-560e-5de2-8152-2dd42e3eff03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={A}^{-1}B\\,d" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0189c759-5807-5750-9382-42a15142e016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-78568/selection/e472aecf20d2cd5f0e251ef5d584b24ad0b47241a56a31d04ed07656c00b18c1" :answer-field/choices ["q-78568/selection/c822a3635f9151eae99cc4f85624072a4ea0b574600ddb4dd37b274d1a11435c" "q-78568/selection/228383024b3593d05de37eed2bb562e0d6a730857df66d9c3955eedff4ae2960" "q-78568/selection/710362311ddc3bc52513e1e2ddc794521971553b13e2205991db2c922f009345" "q-78568/selection/e472aecf20d2cd5f0e251ef5d584b24ad0b47241a56a31d04ed07656c00b18c1" "q-78568/selection/63875f462eaa5a4f7c7dd738a0fe159658214a3db787653ac9c6f2b17eb1d8c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-78568" :question/id #uuid "434e4ac4-2d0e-5134-b4d8-984f36cd5b9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78568" :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${A}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $A{B}^{-1}\\,x=d$ by ${A}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & =d \\\\ {A}^{-1}A{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${B}^{-1}\\,x={A}^{-1}\\,d$ by $B,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1}\\,x & ={A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ B{B}^{-1}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =B{A}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-78568/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5d0cda54-4a4b-5255-b375-ce5e7b604dff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-78568"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-78572"] :question/problem "Consider a matrix equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d,$ where $A$ and $B$ are $5\\times 5$ non-singular matrices, while $x$ and $d$ are $5\\times 1$ column vectors. Solve the equation for $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}\\,x={B}^{-1}\\,d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ {I}_{5}\\,x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d \\\\ x & =A{B}^{-1}\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f5b433aa-17d2-5e91-a08f-3477affa21f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "40398599-c736-5231-83f6-dd91cf084a44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9330039e-54ee-52a6-9da7-c7c1b7494f8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b996bbe6-77e2-52b4-a15a-6bcb715fd96d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "040386b6-5143-5e39-a9e4-c69c7af3cada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e58b42b-ea48-5337-bb06-7cf540036ffb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104536/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-104536/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-104536/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-104536/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-104536/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-104536/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104536" :question/id #uuid "528b601b-5416-5158-83e1-ea8ffb44a5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-104536" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2z=2+2y \\\\ 2y+4z=2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y+z=1 \\\\ 2x-2y-2z=2 \\\\ -2x+2y+4z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-(8-4)+(4-4) \\\\  & =-4+0 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-4}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=2+1+0=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-104536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection/987831c5f76934bed1c525b619b6d103ea696ea5105ab6dc3be7d740d810332a" :answer/id #uuid "bcf8785b-6265-5ef0-83d0-7ea910f09768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=11,y=6,z=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection/e8be7ded28cb08fb20eaf3e07f8442ccd400743c64e91fa3521701e4f00a3f2d" :answer/id #uuid "f4274771-6965-5e28-85ca-7aed5b6b1f78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-11,y=6,z=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection/2dbbe74062c9c15e284211172060371b7b7429912fc6b053cbd9e2ec0b39d388" :answer/id #uuid "b8f212da-c62b-5b55-8dfe-f1bd1c478789" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3,y=-11,z=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection/38967e246ec6580ed591b4273bed57571fc61b5a333504ef3f35656793a255e2" :answer/id #uuid "fd2060ec-2e80-5939-93e4-13de7ea9dbf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=11,y=-6,z=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection/954d79d3a0fb728d4125e8757ab77fe6e0c94b137a806aeb65c23de676b9754d" :answer/id #uuid "acfb8a8b-781e-5d0f-b596-bb531721e814" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=6,y=-3,z=-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "789a32d6-dcb0-5fd8-b255-8b4bfb37e483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104541/selection/38967e246ec6580ed591b4273bed57571fc61b5a333504ef3f35656793a255e2" :answer-field/choices ["q-104541/selection/987831c5f76934bed1c525b619b6d103ea696ea5105ab6dc3be7d740d810332a" "q-104541/selection/e8be7ded28cb08fb20eaf3e07f8442ccd400743c64e91fa3521701e4f00a3f2d" "q-104541/selection/2dbbe74062c9c15e284211172060371b7b7429912fc6b053cbd9e2ec0b39d388" "q-104541/selection/38967e246ec6580ed591b4273bed57571fc61b5a333504ef3f35656793a255e2" "q-104541/selection/954d79d3a0fb728d4125e8757ab77fe6e0c94b137a806aeb65c23de676b9754d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104541" :question/id #uuid "cf9ff59f-8ec8-569a-88c2-1ac3dd73e105" :question/math-academy-id "q-104541" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+z+x=2 \\\\ -3z+y=3 \\\\ 2x+y=4-4z\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We organize the system so that it’s in the correct order first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=2 \\\\ y-3z=3 \\\\ 2x+y+4z=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4+3)-(0+6)+(0-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1\\text{ }\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=11,y=-6,z=-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104541/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104541"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
